{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"5dba6c93d233dbc5","name":"card_event_field_hospital","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/BrothersInArms/events/card_event_field_hospital","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"FIELD HOSPITAL","text":"Fully repair each friendly unit. Draw a card for each unit repaired.","flavorText":"During WWII, US field hospitals played a crucial role in providing medical care to wounded soldiers on the front lines. These field hospitals were mobile units designed to provide emergency medical treatment and stabilize injured personnel before they could be transported to more extensive medical facilities. The United States made several notable contributions and innovations in the field of military medicine during the war. For example the first trials of Mobile Army Surgical Hospitals (MASH) were conducted by the U.S. Army, which was a significant innovation. These mobile surgical hospitals brought advanced surgical capabilities closer to the front lines, reducing the time between injury and surgical intervention. Another innovation was Blood Plasma and Component Therapy which the US military played a crucial role in developing and implementing during the war. This development significantly improved the management of casualties and contributed to better outcomes. It's important to note that while the United States made significant contributions in these areas, other nations also made important advancements in military medicine during WWII. Also note that many medical professionals and researchers from various countries worked together and independently to improve the care and outcomes for wounded soldiers.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_field_hospital","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_field_hospital_title","SourceString":"FIELD HOSPITAL","LocalizedString":"FIELD HOSPITAL"},"Type":"ETypeEnu